OpenROAD: make openroad_lib a public library

bazel-orfs carries this against OpenROAD; it is not upstreamed.

OpenROAD's root BUILD gives `openroad_lib`, the whole tool as one
cc_library, visibility `//:__subpackages__`: only OpenROAD's own
packages may link it. A consumer that wants to write a generator
against odb, utl and sta in its own repository -- bazel-orfs's
tools/structured_gen, which writes placed register files -- can depend
on the public `openroad` binary but not on the library behind it.

This makes `openroad_lib` public and nothing else. It changes no code
and no other target's visibility.

Retires when OpenROAD exposes a library target for embedding; then
`//:bump` onto that commit drops this patch.

--- a/BUILD.bazel	2026-09-17 07:07:02.809732453 +0200
+++ b/BUILD.bazel	2026-09-17 07:07:02.823261141 +0200
@@ -256,7 +256,7 @@
     includes = [
         "include",
     ],
-    visibility = ["//:__subpackages__"],
+    visibility = ["//visibility:public"],
     deps = [
         "//src/gui",
         "//src/sta:opensta_lib",
